{"id":"01a046b0-2037-7dbf-8174-1e4edcd9c4dc","issue_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-i3ym.3","event_type":"closed","actor":"Mark Atwood","old_value":"","new_value":"False positive: The SCHC MIC is a CRC-32 (not a cryptographic MAC) used for transmission error detection per RFC 8724. The value is transmitted in the clear in the All-1 fragment, no secrets are involved, and timing side channels cannot leak anything an attacker does not already know. The project correctly uses constant-time comparison (via subtle crate) for actual security-sensitive operations like Schnorr signature verification.","created_at":"2026-08-28T04:45:42.839902Z"}
